t.post(`${BASE}/api/resource/seed`);\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-346-   not deferred to checkDirectives. Placing destructive tests earlier corrupts state for\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-347-   subsequent tests — this caused 33% of all failures in one observed session. Any test that\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-348-   modifies or deletes shared data (status changes, renames, deletions) MUST either (a)\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:349:   create its own data in `beforeEach` or (b) restore original state in `afterEach`. This\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-350-   prevents 73% of data-contamination failures caused by destructive-ordering.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-351-\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-352-4. **Unique entity names per test.** All test data created by tests (customer names,\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-357-\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-358-5. **TRUNCATE before seeding (Neon branches).** Seed scripts MUST call `truncateAllTables()`\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-359-   before inserting data. Neon branch creation inherits parent data, so insert-only seeding\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:360:   produces duplicates. Always use `truncateAndSeed()`, never `seedDatabase()` alone.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-361-\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-362-6. **Relative or data-independent assertions.** Tests that verify data after mutations must\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-363-   query current state before the action and assert relative changes, not absolute values.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-364-\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-365-7. **Status transition tests must reset state.** Tests that change entity status (e.g., RFI\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:366:   status, submittal status) MUST include `beforeEach` API calls to reset the entity back to\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-367-   its initial state. Without this, status transition tests leave entities in terminal states\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-368-   that break subsequent tests. In one session, this pattern caused 14 affected tests across\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-369-   RFI and submittal status spec files.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-370-\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-371-8. **Distinct test data records per test.** Each test must operate on its own database\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-372-   record (vendor, PO, delivery, etc.) rather than sharing records across tests. Every spec\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:373:   file should create its own test data via API calls in `beforeEach`/`beforeAll` rather\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-374-   than relying on seed data. This is the single highest-impact isolation improvement —\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-375-   57.8% of observed failures came from data contamination when tests shared seed data.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-376-   In one session, this single change would have prevented 10+ data-contamination failures\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-377-   across receive-delivery, vendor-detail, and PO-related spec files.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-378-\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md-379-   **State reset for destructive operations**: Every `describe` block containing tests that\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:380:   perform destructive operations (delete, modify, toggle) MUST include a `beforeEach` or\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:381:   `beforeAll` hook that resets state to a known baseline. Without this, earlier tests that\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-382-   delete or modify entities corrupt state for subsequent tests. This single practice would\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-383-   have prevented 4 data-contamination clusters (22 affected tests) in one observed session.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-384-\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-395-    changes a user's password MUST restore the original password in `afterAll` or use a\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-396-    dedicated test user account. Password mutations cascade into 18+ failures across other\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-397-    spec files (e.g., personal-info, messages) that rely on the original credentials for\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:398:    API authentication and `beforeEach` cleanup. This is the highest-blast-radius\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-399-    data-contamination pattern observed — a single password change can break 3+ spec files.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-400-\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-401-12. **Navigate before `page.evaluate(fetch(...))`**. Tests that use `page.evaluate(fetch(...))`\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:402:   for API-driven setup in `beforeEach` or `beforeAll` MUST call `page.goto()` first to\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md-403-   navigate to the app. `fetch()` with relative URLs fails at `about:blank` because there\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-404-   is no base URL to resolve against. Always ensure the page has navigated before making\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-405-   fetch calls via `page.evaluate`.\n--\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md-420-   named `route-stop-list`. Use `:not()` exclusions or more specific selectors to avoid\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-421-   overcounting.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-422-\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:423:14. **Mandatory beforeEach cleanup in ALL spec files that modify data.** Every spec file\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:424:    that creates, updates, or deletes records MUST include a `beforeEach` hook that resets\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-425-    the relevant data to seed state via API calls. This is a writing-time requirement, not\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-426-    a fixTests concern. Data contamination accounted for 54% of all test failures in one\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-427-    observed session (62.9% test isolation score). Do not wait for contamination to occur\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:428:    before adding cleanup — add it proactively from the start.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-429-\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-430-15. **Use `test.describe.serial` as the default for all spec files.** Since all tests share\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-431-    a database branch, parallel execution within a spec file causes data-contamination\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-435-16. **Shared test utility for seed data reset.** When the same API-based reset logic is\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-436-    needed across multiple spec files (e.g., `resetPayments()`, `resetOrderStatuses()`),\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-437-    extract it to a shared test utility file (e.g., `tests/helpers/reset.ts`). This\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:438:    reduces boilerplate and ensures consistent cleanup across all spec files. The\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-439-    `destructive-test-reordering` pattern was applied identically across 4 spec files in\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-440-    one session — a shared `resetDatabase(resource)` helper would have prevented this\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-441-    duplication.\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-455-    `items`) silently fails to delete anything, corrupting database state for subsequent tests.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-456-    This was the direct cause of member table corruption in one observed session.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-457-\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:458:19. **Reseed tables in FK dependency order.** When reseeding multiple tables in `beforeEach`\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-459-    hooks, respect foreign key constraints by seeding parent tables before child tables. For\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md-460-    example: `instructors → members → bookings` (members reference instructors, bookings\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-461-    reference members). Calling reseed endpoints in the wrong order causes FK constraint\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-462-    violations that look like application bugs but are actually test infrastructure issues.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-463-\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:464:20. **Mandatory `beforeAll` truncateAndSeed.** Every spec file MUST include a `beforeAll`\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:465:    hook that calls `truncateAndSeed` to ensure a clean database state before the spec runs.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-466-    This prevents cross-run data accumulation — the single largest sub-category of\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-467-    data-contamination failures (57% of data-contamination, 40% of all failures in one\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:468:    session). The `beforeEach` cleanup in mandate #1 handles within-run contamination;\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:469:    this `beforeAll` handles cross-run contamination from prior test executions against the\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-470-    same Neon branch.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-471-\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-472-21. **Post-destructive re-seeding in serial blocks.** Any test that deletes all records\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-484-## Pre-Commit Checklist for New Spec Files\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-485-\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md-486-Before committing a new spec file, verify:\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:487:- No test creates, modifies, or deletes shared data without cleanup or isolation.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-488-- Destructive tests (delete-all, empty-state) are in `test.describe.serial` at the end.\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:489:- Status transition tests include `beforeEach` state resets.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-490-- Created records use unique identifiers (`Date.now()`, `crypto.randomUUID()`).\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-491-- Count assertions use flexible matching (`toBeGreaterThan`) or relative counts.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-492-\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-524-  calls (e.g., expecting exactly 1 fetch) will see 2. Use `waitFor` patterns that assert on\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-525-  DOM state rather than counting network requests.\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md-526-- **Race conditions**: Two concurrent fetches for the same data can cause state flicker or\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:527:  stale data display. Components should handle this with cleanup functions in useEffect\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-528-  (abort controllers) or by ignoring stale responses.\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md-529-- **Test flakiness**: If tests assert on intermediate render states, StrictMode's extra\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-530-  render cycle can cause intermittent failures. Always wait for the final stable state\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-619-  restart the dev server before re-running tests. The dev server may cache old function bundles.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-620-  Kill background processes with `pkill -f \"netlify\"` and `pkill -f \"vite\"` before restarting.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-621-\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:622:- When a checkDirectives finding suggests removing test code (e.g., \"redundant\" cleanup,\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-623-  \"unnecessary\" helpers), always run the affected tests *before* committing the removal to\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-624-  confirm the change is safe. Cleanup code that looks redundant may be essential for test\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-625-  isolation.\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-672-\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-673-- Always run tests via `npm run test <testFile>` (from the app directory), never by calling\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-674-  `npx playwright test` directly. The test script includes essential pre-test setup (branch\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:675:  creation, schema init, seeding, stale cleanup) that is skipped when running Playwright directly.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-676-\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-677-## Tips\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-678-\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-707-  Playwright `webServer` config starts fresh processes on different ports and is not affected.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-708-- **Kill stale processes before every test run.** Port conflicts from stale `netlify dev`\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-709-  processes are a significant source of infrastructure failures (20 events affecting 225 test\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:710:  runs in one observed session). Always run the pre-flight cleanup (`pkill -f \"netlify|vite\"`,\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-711-  `fuser -k 8888/tcp`) before each test run, not just the first run in a session.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-712-- Commit incrementally during debugging sessions. If you improve test results (e.g., 81→207 passing)\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-713-  or fix a meaningful issue, commit those changes immediately even if other failures remain. An\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-734-  previous tests. Each test starts with a fresh seed.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-735-- Seed scripts must always call `truncateAllTables()` (or equivalent) before inserting data\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-736-  to ensure idempotency. Without truncation, re-running seeds causes duplicate key errors.\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:737:  Every test file's `beforeAll`/`beforeEach` should TRUNCATE relevant tables before inserting\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-738-  seed data, not just delete known IDs. Hardcoded ID deletion breaks when Neon branches\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:739:  inherit data from parent branches. **Always use `truncateAndSeed()`, never `seedDatabase()`\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-740-  alone** — Neon ephemeral branches inherit parent data, so insert-only seeding produces\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-741-  duplicates.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-742-- The Vite dev server cold start can cause the first test in a suite to timeout. Consider adding\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:743:  a warm-up navigation in `beforeAll` or increasing the first test's timeout to account for\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-744-  cold start latency.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-745-- Avoid hardcoding expected values in assertions. Tests that hardcode specific counts (e.g.,\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-746-  `expect 1 remaining task`) or specific names (e.g., `\"David Lee\"`) break when test data\n--\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-897-  (e.g., `visit_type`, `status`), verify them against the database schema's CHECK constraints\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-898-  or enum definitions. Invalid enum values cause constraint violations that surface as cryptic\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-899-  500 errors. This pattern appeared in 2+ spec files in observed sessions.\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:900:- Any test that creates records (orders, customers, etc.) should include a `beforeEach`\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:901:  cleanup helper (e.g., `deleteAllOrders()`) to prevent data accumulation across tests.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-902-  Add this from the start when writing tests — don't wait for contamination failures.\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:903:- **Reset global settings in beforeEach.** Since settings are typically a single-row table,\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-904-  any spec that tests settings modifications (business name, preferences, etc.) should reset\nskills/tasks/build/testing.md:905:  settings to known defaults in a `beforeEach` hook via API call. Otherwise, earlier tests\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-906-  that modify settings will contaminate later tests in the same file.\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-907-- Any test that deletes all records (e.g., empty state tests) must be in a\n/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md-908-  `test.describe.serial` block at the end of the describe. Destructive tests placed earlier","numLines":233}}
